error[E1002]: `xs` goes `mut` in a call evaluated while `xs` is lent `mut`
  --> mem:///main.lu:23:9
   |
22 |     (mut xs).push({
   |     -------- `xs` is the call's `mut` receiver here
23 |         (mut xs).push(7)
   |         ^^^^^^^^ a second claim inside the outer call's extent
   |
   = note: the same place twice is never disjoint. A `mut` argument is exclusive for the whole
     call, and the arguments after it are evaluated inside that claim [mem.tier0.excl]. A
     `mut` receiver is the call's first argument. Evaluate the inner call into a local BEFORE
     the outer one.

